Why this structure: The process produces a neutral version alongside a record of what changed, so a reviewer can see exactly what was altered and why. The substance step is first because it protects against the failure of ignoring the input. Rule 1 is the key rule: it says how to neutralize a bias without silently treating a biased claim as true.

Technique: Zero-shot with an explicit taxonomy of issue types. The taxonomy gives the model a consistent vocabulary, which matters more than examples here.

Failure modes prevented:

Refusal or ignoring the input, which the substance step blocks.
Sanitizing away the grievance, which the “preserve every substantive point” rule blocks.
Moralizing, which the “do not lecture” line blocks.
Passing bias through the summary. The objective version is required to mark generalizations rather than repeat them as fact.
Emotional content swaying the output. Emotional intensifiers are explicitly classified and rewritten.